énéfice du packing.", "evidence_ids": ["20d5d3610fd14da9"]}], "read": {"evidence_id": "", "offset": 0, "operation": "none", "path": ""}, "uncertainties": ["Les sources détaillées des variantes T2 ne sont pas visibles ici; leurs différences précises de noyau et de packing restent inconnues.", "Les temps par taille et les résultats des cinq répétitions confirmatoires ne sont pas visibles pour les essais T2."]}, "report_id": "active-analyst-7a1a8e976b894c7a870e8c3fca5896d9", "status": "complete", "watermark": ["4184453b5e7a41a6", "132b8ca4ab774f70", "5bf16cd2c3b8448f", "327ada26fd134727"]}}, "memory": {"schema": "hpc-forest-memory-v1", "enabled": true, "scope": {"epoch": 1, "protocol_id": "2d33d81cdcfbbc0125107dd390bec575ba5a2ce3cdcf202e3523a21b61c661cb", "tree_id": null}, "page": {"schema": "hpc-forest-memory-v1", "items": [{"id": "30462536c13c4e5d", "kind": "experiment", "role": "Gm1", "tree_id": "e1:Gm1", "mission_id": "30462536c13c4e5d", "facts": {"commit": "2556f8effe9d1d1f8ee6297517b1466e98fe4958", "base_commit": "359c83cd5e093c1682fec2365f7f375dc7dd2b15", "parent_id": null, "source_ids": ["4184453b5e7a41a6", "20d5d3610fd14da9"], "source_count": 2, "source_change": {"available": true, "kind": "nonconfiguration_files_changed", "changed_file_count": 1, "configuration_file_count": 0, "semantic_novelty": "not_established_by_file_hashes", "identical_input_ids": [], "identical_input_count": 0}}, "measured_outcome": {"status": "valid", "correct": true, "mean_seconds": 0.0034172374333333332, "score": 0.9994019923296508}, "diagnostic": "", "model_interpretation": {"claim": "Le noyau SIMD AVX-512 et le chemin de panneaux empaquetés de T2 sont déjà plus rapides que T1 pris seul. Pour les petites dimensions non empaquetées, le lancement de l'équipe OpenMP et le parcours parallèle collapse(2) peuvent coûter plus que le calcul. Appliquer la politique sérielle de T1 sous n=256 tout en conservant le micro-noyau SIMD pourrait réduire ce surcoût; seule la mesure contrôleur dira si cela compense d'éventuelles pertes à n=128.", "transformations": "{"files":["src/candidate.cpp"],"retained":["Conserver le noyau SIMD AVX-512 à dispatch d'exécution, son repli scalaire et le chemin T2 de panneaux B empaquetés pour les grandes dimensions.","Dans le chemin direct n<256, remplacer la région OpenMP collapse(2) par le parcours sériel des mêmes tuiles 8x16, reprenant la politique sérielle de T1 pour les petits cas; tous les autres chemins restent inchangés."]}", "applicability": "", "next_experiment": "", "evidence_ids": []}, "source_available": true, "details_are_bounded": true}, {"id": "fb2b011885c849d7", "kind": "experiment", "role": "Gm2", "tree_id": "e1:Gm2", "mission_id": "fb2b011885c849d7", "facts": {"commit": "fcecec9ec9afd614455a72a5fabe42ffa3fb0e58", "base_commit": "18b77394715a712d096a7d2ec4182ed14235491c", "parent_id": null, "source_ids": ["5bf16cd2c3b8448f", "30462536c13c4e5d"], "source_count": 2, "source_change": {"available": true, "kind": "nonconfiguration_files_changed", "changed_file_count": 1, "configuration_file_count": 0, "semantic_novelty": "not_established_by_file_hashes", "identical_input_ids": [], "identical_input_count": 0}}, "measured_outcome": {"status": "valid", "correct": true, "mean_seconds": 0.002788934231481481, "score": 0.9995118900888018}, "diagnostic": "", "model_interpretation": {"claim": "Le changement Gm1 (parcours direct sériel sous n=256) peut réduire le coût de lancement pour les petits cas, mais son résultat agrégé antérieur est légèrement plus lent que T2 et ne démontre pas de gain à n=1024. Pour tester une composition pertinente à n=1024, je conserve ce parcours et remplace le packing B sériel du panneau par un omp for statique sur ses lignes K, avec une ligne exclusive par itération et la même barrière avant le micro-noyau. Cela peut réduire le chemin critique de packing, mais le coût de synchronisation peut annuler le gain; correction et vitesse restent à mesurer.", "transformations": "{"files":["src/candidate.cpp"],"retained":["Conserver le noyau AVX-512/FMA 8x16 à dispatch d’exécution, le repli scalaire, les panneaux et le GEMM générique de T2.","Adopter la traversée sérielle des tuiles SIMD directes pour n<256 de Gm1; le repli direct en cas d’échec d’allocation reste parallèle.","Dans le chemin empaqueté, remplacer le packing B sous omp single par un omp for schedule(static) sur les lignes K, avec écritures disjointes et barrière implicite avant le calcul; garder l’ordre K, les dimensions de panneaux et les tuiles de sortie."]}", "applicability": "", "next_experiment": "", "evidence_ids": []}, "source_available": true, "details_are_bounded": true}, {"id": "1ebc3c277286431d", "kind": "experiment", "role": "T1", "tree_id": "e1:T1", "mission_id": "1ebc3c277286431d", "facts": {"commit": "e1ed1f1a7afabd7a3b50d99c7d14927acb6a8e76", "base_commit": "37fde83d1a31400b6879cdca015746966ad9d942", "parent_id": null, "source_ids": [], "source_count": 0, "source_change": {"available": true, "kind": "nonconfiguration_files_changed", "changed_file_count": 1, "configuration_file_count": 0, "semantic_novelty": "not_established_by_file_hashes", "identical_input_ids": [], "identical_input_count": 0}}, "measured_outcome": {"status": "valid", "correct": true, "mean_seconds": 0.01619630738095238, "score": 0.9971720125379574}, "diagnostic": "", "model_interpretation": {"claim": "The supplied T1 candidates are all valid and have repeated aggregate means of 0.01140523 s (4x256x16), 0.01587444 s (8x128x32), and 0.02015676 s (8x64x32), but no per-size timings are available to attribute a result specifically to n=1024. This contrasting 4x128x16 scheme assigns independent row/column output tiles under static OpenMP scheduling, potentially improving cache residency and work distribution at large sizes; the smaller tiles and extra tile-loop work may instead hurt. It retains serial execution below n=256 and contiguous i-k-j output-column updates.", "transformations": "{"files":["src/candidate.cpp"],"retained":["Replace fixed-size dispatch with generic handling for every positive n and zero the complete output before accumulation.","Use unpacked 4x128x16 row/column/K tiles with ascending K blocks and an i-k-j update whose innermost output-column loop is contiguous.","Assign disjoint row/column output tiles with static collapsed OpenMP scheduling for n >= 256; run serially below that threshold or when only one worker is requested.","Clamp the requested worker count to the range 1..8; do not pack matrices or use explicit intrinsics."]}", "applicability": "", "next_experiment": "", "evidence_ids": []}, "source_available": true, "details_are_bounded": true}, {"id": "52c15139e2464dfa", "kind": "experiment", "role": "T2", "tree_id": "e1:T2", "mission_id": "52c15139e2464dfa", "facts": {"commit": "1d52fdd1529dba6722ab201df36665dff7273322", "base_commit": "359c83cd5e093c1682fec2365f7f375dc7dd2b15", "parent_id": "4184453b5e7a41a6", "source_ids": [], "source_count": 0, "source_change": {"available": true, "kind": "nonconfiguration_files_changed", "changed_file_count": 1, "configuration_file_count": 0, "semantic_novelty": "not_established_by_file_hashes", "identical_input_ids": [], "identical_input_count": 0}}, "measured_outcome": {"status": "valid", "correct": true, "mean_seconds": 0.003459756584674329, "score": 0.9993945560936134}, "diagnostic": "", "model_interpretation": {"claim": "Building on selected parent 4184453b5e7a41a6, keep its 8-row AVX-512 FMA kernel family, B-only 128x128 packing, KC/NC, threshold, and OpenMP ownership, but widen NR from 16 to 32. One A broadcast can then feed two column vectors and the wider tile may reduce per-row-block tile overhead; the additional accumulators may instead increase register pressure. This isolates tile width without assuming it improves n=1024 performance.", "transformations": "{"files":["src/candidate.cpp"],"retained":["Widened the explicit AVX-512 microkernel from 8x16 to 8x32, using two 16-lane vectors and reusing each 